course: dictionary
lesson: 15325
title: Sniffle and the sniffles
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A sniffle is a small sound made through the nose. You can sniffle because you have a cold, or because you are crying quietly. Context shows you which one. «Lily sniffled as she read the sad letter» tells you she is upset, not poorly, because of the sad letter.
explain: «Ben has the sniffles, but he still wants to go to school.» Here the sniffles is a noun, and it means a mild cold with a runny nose. The clue is «but he still wants to go to school»: a mild cold does not usually keep you at home. Words like this are often informal, so you will hear them at home and in playgrounds more than in books.
explain: Try swapping your meaning into the sentence. If you read «Lily sniffed again and again because she was crying quietly», the sentence still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning. Sniffle is also a verb with endings: sniffles, sniffled, sniffling.
fact: Sniffle is a verb: to sniff again and again, because you have a cold or are crying quietly.
fact: The sniffles (informal) means a mild cold with a runny nose: «Ben has the sniffles.»
fact: Sniffling is also a noun for the sound of sniffing: «The room was quiet except for sniffling.»
fact: Health rule: use a tissue, catch it, bin it, kill it. «Please sniffle into a tissue, not your sleeve.»
fact: In stories, a character who sniffles is often sad or trying not to cry, so read the words around it for clues.
exercise: «Lily sniffled as she read the sad letter from her best friend.» What does sniffled mean here? | *Sniffed again and again, because she was crying quietly | Ran fast out of the room | Laughed loudly at a joke | Ate her lunch in a hurry
exercise: «Ben has the sniffles, but he still wants to go to school.» What are the sniffles? | *A mild cold with a runny nose | A type of school lunch | Very serious illness that needs a hospital | A bad fall in the playground
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means to sniff again and again: «Please sniffle into a tissue, not your sleeve.» | sleeve | please | tissue | *sniffle
test: Maya has the sniffles and a runny nose. What is wrong with Maya? | A broken arm | Hungry after lunch | A sprained ankle | *A mild cold
test: «Please sniffle into a tissue, not your sleeve.» What should you do with the tissue afterwards? | Keep it in your pocket for later | *Bin it | Hide it under your bed | Share it with a friend
exam: In a story, «The little boy sniffled quietly in the corner.» What does sniffled most likely show? | Excitement about a party | He is running a race | He is very cold and hungry | *He is sad or trying not to cry
